# Source and experiment notes — not reader-facing draft

Source basis: `thesis/07-hko-local-maximum.tex`; `07-hko-local-maximum-chart-reduction.tex`; `07-hko-local-maximum-exact-certificate.tex`; ratio/symmetry definitions located in `02-preliminaries-ehz-capacity.tex`.

Limits: This is an exposition candidate derived from those sources, not an independent verification of the certificate or chart lemma. Twenty-six touching bounds is exact source content; no claim that they exhaust optimizers. The symplectic-convention equivalence is compressed to a statement and needs the surrounding convention discussion or a short reference in the integrated chapter. No explicit neighborhood radius is claimed. The HKO counterexample is prior work; the local theorem is the contribution presented here.

Schematic worth considering: a two-dimensional analogy showing several smooth upper surfaces touching at one point, their lower envelope decreasing in every direction, beside a small derivative-row diagram with the origin inside their convex hull. Label explicitly as an analogy to the twenty-five-dimensional slice; do not draw one capacity branch or suggest differentiability of the true ratio. The envelope bounds the true ratio from above; it is not asserted to equal it.
